meta {
  name: 68 Share and Inform E2E
  seq: 68
}

docs {
  End-to-end, DEPENDENT chain for the Order Console "Share and Inform" feature:
  send a patient their lab report over SMS / Email / WhatsApp, reusing the
  communication module. Run the requests top-to-bottom (Bruno "Run Folder", or
  one by one) — each captures a variable the next needs.

  Flow:
    01 SiteAdmin Login              → siteAdminToken
    02-04 SiteAdmin: create GLOBAL messaging templates (SMS/Email/WhatsApp),
          feature = console_lab_report_as_attachment → share*GlobalId
    05 Business Login               → businessAccessToken
    06 Business: create an active lab_all_report PDF template (so Email/WhatsApp
       can render + attach the report PDF)                → labAllReportTemplateId
    07-09 Business: ACTIVATE each global (clone into tenant)
    10 Business: list orders → pick one                    → shareOrderId
    11 Get Share Info (preload: patient contacts + which channels are activated)
    12 Share via SMS   (text-only, needs only a patient mobile — the sure path)
    13 Share via Email (attaches the lab_all_report PDF)
    14 Share via WhatsApp (attaches the PDF)
    15 List communications → confirm the queued rows

  The feature's own NEW endpoints are just TWO: GET .../share-info (step 11, the
  popup preload) and POST .../share (steps 12-14, one per channel). Everything
  else reuses existing template/order/communication APIs.

  WHAT ACTUALLY REACHES THE RECIPIENT (important):
    - EMAIL  → really delivers. No carrier registration needed. Set your inbox in
      step 13 (`shareTestEmail`) and you'll receive it (with the PDF).
    - SMS / WhatsApp → the API + relay ACCEPT them (status SENT, exchange_id set),
      but a real phone only receives them if the template's provider ids are REAL:
      SMS needs a DLT-registered smsTemplateId + smsSenderId (and body matching the
      DLT text); WhatsApp needs a Meta/AiSensy-APPROVED template id. The steps ship
      with PLACEHOLDER ids so the flow runs green end-to-end (guard passes, relay
      accepts) — replace them with your real provider ids to get actual handset
      delivery. Until then, SMS/WhatsApp will show SENT but won't arrive on a phone.

  Notes:
    - SMS/WhatsApp DELIVERY needs carrier registration: set real provider ids in
      steps 02 (smsDltTemplateId + smsSenderId) and 04 (whatsappTemplateId +
      whatsappSenderId) BEFORE creating the globals — the clone in 07-09 copies
      them into the tenant. Missing them → 422 SHARE_TEMPLATE_NOT_CONFIGURED on
      share (the relay would otherwise accept + the carrier silently drop).
      Re-activating after editing a global: delete the stale tenant clone first
      (DELETE /templates/:id), since clone is idempotent and won't overwrite.
    - A channel only works if its global template was activated (07-09). Skipping
      activation → 422 SHARE_TEMPLATE_NOT_ACTIVATED (that's the gate working).
    - Email/WhatsApp additionally need the order to HAVE lab reports (accepted
      samples) AND an active lab_all_report template (step 06); otherwise the PDF
      render throws ORDER_REPORTS_NOT_FOUND / NO_ACTIVE_PRINT_TEMPLATE. SMS has no
      such dependency.
    - Set your real login creds in steps 01 and 05 (pre-request vars) if the
      defaults don't match your environment.
}
